1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,878
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:08,216
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,299 --> 00:00:10,677
- ♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,804
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:15,724
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:20,020
- [Dmitri] Just because I treated you well
- [mid-tempo music playing]

7
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,313
doesn't mean you're the one
I want for my daughter.

8
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:23,898
He doesn't want us to be together.

9
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:26,484
Didn't Audrey object?

10
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:27,652
[Atoy] She doesn't know, Godmother.

11
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:28,945
She doesn't know yet.

12
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:32,949
You should have finished off
that Atoy long ago,

13
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,868
so I wouldn't be worrying now!

14
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:37,746
You keep giving me problems, Red!

15
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:39,664
[in English] Let me correct my mistake.

16
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:44,961
[Mercado] <i>A terrorist group</i>
<i>known as Obsidian is reportedly training</i>

17
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:46,796
<i>here in the Philippines.</i>

18
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,339
‪PREVIOUSLY

19
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:51,718
[receptionist, in English]
How can I help you, sir?

20
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:52,886
Sokolov.

21
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:55,930
[in English] Mr. Alexei Sokolov.

22
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:58,224
[in English] My brother, Andrei.

23
00:00:58,308 --> 00:00:59,809
Andrei Sokolov.

24
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,478
[receptionist, in English]
Here are your access cards.

25
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:03,897
[in English] Thank you.

26
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:08,026
[Mercado] <i>But your mission</i>
<i>is to retrieve a laptop containing</i>

27
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:11,071
<i>the location of the camps.</i>

28
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:14,199
[Samir, in English] Stop!

29
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,369
[in English] What is your name?

30
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:21,581
[in English] We are the Sokolov brothers.

31
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:23,166
[in English] You are brothers?

32
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:24,167
Uh-huh.

33
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,168
[in English] You two?

34
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:26,211
[Atoy] Hm-mm.

35
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:37,096
[in English] Okay, brothers,
you can proceed to the waiting area.

36
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:39,891
[in English] The ambassador
is still in a meeting.

37
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:40,850
[in English] Oh.

38
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:45,021
[in English] We, uh… We are also here
for, uh, for meeting.

39
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:45,939
[in English] Yes.

40
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:47,649
[in English] You are early, sir.

41
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:52,487
[in English] Well, you know what they say,
"Early bird catches worm."

42
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:56,074
[laughing]

43
00:01:56,157 --> 00:01:57,826
Uh, because worm…

44
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:01,371
- Uh, we're early, and the birds…
- [mutters]

45
00:02:01,454 --> 00:02:03,873
- [indistinct chattering]
- Very good. Very good.

46
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:04,791
‪[quirky sting]

47
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:06,584
[in English] This way.

48
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,134
[music fades]

49
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:18,471
[in Russian] The Maldives is beautiful.
[in English] I plan to put a resort there.

50
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:19,889
[in Russian] Seriously?

51
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,641
[man 3, in Russian]
I was there last month.

52
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:24,102
[man 1, in English]
You're here for the meeting?

53
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:25,061
[Atoy] Hmm?

54
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:27,021
Uh…

55
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,273
[in English] Uh, yes, yes.

56
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:29,774
[device blips]

57
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:31,609
[in English] What business are you into?

58
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:33,862
[in English] Oh, uh…

59
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:35,822
[clicks tongue, in English] Textiles.

60
00:02:35,905 --> 00:02:37,448
[device blips]

61
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:40,451
[speaking in Russian]

62
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:41,995
[in English] Thank you.

63
00:02:43,121 --> 00:02:45,915
[in English] Uh… I made it myself.

64
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:50,628
[suspicious music playing]

65
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:59,012
[in English] The ambassador will see
you now. Please come with me.

66
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:00,889
[speaks in Russian]

67
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:06,019
[music swells]

68
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,106
- [Atoy groans]
- [soft rock music playing]

69
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:13,234
Atoy, Atoy, your neck!

70
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:15,403
- Oh, it's coming off.
- [gasps]

71
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:16,696
Hey, you're right.

72
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:20,867
[Atoy muttering]

73
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:22,785
[Atoy groans]

74
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:25,580
- Okay? Is that okay?
- That's okay, oh-- [grunts]

75
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:28,791
[Samir, in English] Mr. Sokolov,
what is happening here?

76
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:31,377
[rousing music playing]

77
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:36,257
[suave theme music playing]

78
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,159
[music fades]

79
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:05,036
[Kurt, in English] Oh, yes?

80
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:06,162
[in English] Can I help you?

81
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,997
[in English] No. I should
be asking that question.

82
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:10,124
[in English] What are you doing
to your brother?

83
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:11,334
- [mutters]
- [in English] Why are you choking him?

84
00:04:11,417 --> 00:04:13,211
[chuckles, in English] No, no.
[in Russian] No, no. He…

85
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:16,297
[in English] He has
a bad rash on his neck.

86
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,216
[in English] It's something itchy.

87
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,510
- [in English] Sir, are you okay?
- [Kurt] No. [stammers]

88
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:21,803
[grunts]

89
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:24,931
[in English] Sorry. I apologize.
My mistake. I--

90
00:04:25,014 --> 00:04:26,599
[in English] You, my friend,
are too close.

91
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:28,810
- [in English] I will talk to your brother.
- [in English] Yes, yes, yes. Okay, yes.

92
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:30,478
- [in English] Of course, yes, yes.
- [in English] I will talk to your brother.

93
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:32,480
[in English] Very good, very-- Ah, yes.

94
00:04:32,563 --> 00:04:34,691
[in English] What is happening here?
What is going on?

95
00:04:34,774 --> 00:04:36,234
- [sneaky music playing]
- [Kurt mutters]

96
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:39,153
- Uh…
- [chuckles] Uh…

97
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,322
[in English] Is there something
wrong with your neck, sir?

98
00:04:42,156 --> 00:04:46,577
[in English] No. I, uh…
I just dropped my, uh, pen.

99
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:50,373
[in English] I use it for, uh…
Yes. Itchy, itchy. Yes.

100
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:51,416
[in English] Allergy.

101
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:55,586
[in English] Okay. You two, come with me.

102
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:56,879
[Atoy, in English] No, no, no, no.

103
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:59,924
- [music fades]
- [in English] My brother will stay.

104
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:02,093
[in English] He's, um,
not feeling well. Right?

105
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:04,262
[in English] I-I will--
I will go with you.

106
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:07,015
[groans, in English] Yes.

107
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:10,101
[in English] Bad oysters
from last night. It's--

108
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:11,769
- [in English] Okay. You stay here.
- [in English] Relax, brother.

109
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:13,187
[groans]

110
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:14,814
- [in English] Come, let's go.
- [in English] Shall we?

111
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:15,732
- [in English] Yes. Follow me.
- [Kurt sighs]

112
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:20,778
[soft rock music playing]

113
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:25,283
[music fades]

114
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:39,797
[suspicious music playing]

115
00:05:39,881 --> 00:05:45,887
[line ringing]

116
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:54,103
[Gavin, in English] Where's my phone?

117
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:55,396
There! [clicks tongue]

118
00:05:56,647 --> 00:05:57,732
[sighs]

119
00:05:58,524 --> 00:06:01,110
[music fades]

120
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:02,278
[in English] Auntie, are you okay?

121
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:06,741
[in English] No.

122
00:06:07,533 --> 00:06:08,743
[in English] I'm not okay.

123
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:12,580
I haven't heard from Atoy
since our dinner here at home.

124
00:06:12,663 --> 00:06:17,376
Perhaps Brother Atoy is just really busy.
Maybe he has a lot of orders at his shop.

125
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:22,882
[in English] Or he could simply
just be ghosting you.

126
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:26,094
[sinister music playing]

127
00:06:26,177 --> 00:06:27,637
Why would he do that?

128
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,098
Atoy isn't like that.

129
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:35,978
And besides, we already have a child,
and we've built our family.

130
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:39,357
[tense music playing]

131
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:53,329
[in English] Fyodor Orlov, Mr. Ambassador.

132
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:55,915
[in English] My name is Ivan, Ivan Petrov.

133
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:57,917
[in Russian] I'm Pyotr Lebedev.

134
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,712
[suspicious music playing]

135
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:06,342
[Viktor, in English] You are new here.

136
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:08,177
[in English] I have not seen your face.

137
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:09,262
Uh…

138
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:12,640
[in English] Viktor Petrov,
ambassador of Zahran.

139
00:07:12,723 --> 00:07:17,186
[in English] Mr. Ambassador,
I am Alexei Sokolov, sir.

140
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,147
[in English] Please, sit.

141
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:21,065
[Atoy sighs]

142
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:25,403
[in English] So,
you are the elder Sokolov brother?

143
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:28,573
- [in English] That's right.
- [Viktor, in English] I'm glad you came.

144
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:33,035
[in English] But, uh,
where is your brother now?

145
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:36,080
[sneaky music playing]

146
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:51,554
[gasps, in English] Yes?
Uh… I am, uh, Andrei Sokolov.

147
00:07:51,637 --> 00:07:53,723
[in English] I am, uh…
I'm just getting water.

148
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:57,018
[in English] Just drinking water.
There's nothing wrong with that, huh?

149
00:07:57,101 --> 00:07:59,687
[in English] Of course, sir.
Uh, is everything okay?

150
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:02,607
[in English] Uh, don't worry.
You seem a little nervous.

151
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,400
[in English] Just relax.

152
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:07,653
One of the Sokolovs is here.
What could he be doing?

153
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:10,615
[in English] I'm just, uh,
waiting for my brother. Hmm?

154
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:13,951
Do you understand Tagalog?
Are you really a foreigner?

155
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:16,704
[sneaky music playing]

156
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:19,624
[in English] Actually, uh, yes.
A little bit, a little bit.

157
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:21,459
Uh, uh… [sighs]

158
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,879
[in English] You know, it's a long story.

159
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:27,840
[in English] I was separated
from my brother when we were young,

160
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,176
you know, and I love him so much.

161
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:34,305
[in English] I ended up here
in the Philippines.

162
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:38,184
[in English] Oh, I thought I would
never see my brother again!

163
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:40,895
[sobs, in English] It's so sad.

164
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,438
[in English] But then, he found me!

165
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:46,400
[in English] And I'm so happy.
I have a brother again!

166
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:48,236
[in English] A whole family.

167
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,779
[laughs]

168
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:51,864
[in English] Congratulations, sir.

169
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:53,324
We are happy for you.

170
00:08:53,407 --> 00:08:57,036
[chuckles, in English]
Thank you, thank you, comrades.

171
00:08:57,912 --> 00:08:58,788
[in English] Okay.

172
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,171
[Atoy, in English] <i>Oh, he's just outside.</i>

173
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:09,799
[in English] Talking to some girls.

174
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:11,592
- [Viktor] Oh!
- [sneaky chuckle]

175
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,052
- [sneaky music playing]
- [laughs]

176
00:09:13,135 --> 00:09:16,681
[in English] So, he's a ladies' man,

177
00:09:16,764 --> 00:09:19,559
and you are the businessman
of the family, yes?

178
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:21,018
Ha!

179
00:09:22,853 --> 00:09:24,647
[in English] I like your style.

180
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,857
[in English] It's very refreshing.

181
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,067
- [scoffs]
- [Atoy chuckles]

182
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:31,028
[in English] He is in the business
of textiles, that is why.

183
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:32,238
Ah!

184
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:33,698
[Viktor, in English] No wonder.

185
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:37,201
- [Viktor, in English] Very nice.
- [in English] Thank you.

186
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:38,828
[suspicious music playing]

187
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:40,204
- [in English] Oh
- [indistinct].

188
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:43,874
[speaking in Russian]

189
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,126
[Viktor, in English] Please.

190
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:48,254
- [Viktor, in English] Please sit.
- [device blips]

191
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:55,970
[clears throat]

192
00:09:59,807 --> 00:10:01,475
- [blipping]
- [Mercado, in English] Oh, you found it!

193
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:03,144
That's our target.

194
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:05,479
You can really be relied on, Padua.

195
00:10:06,355 --> 00:10:09,150
If you have the chance
to get it now, do it.

196
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:12,278
But make sure you won't be compromised.

197
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:17,158
[in English] No need to answer.
Just do it if you can.

198
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:19,368
[soft rock music playing]

199
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:23,623
I'LL SEE IF I CAN MOVE
TOWARDS THE OBJECTIVE NOW, SIR

200
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:25,291
Samir.

201
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:28,377
[pensive music playing]

202
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:30,546
[in English] Bring this to my office.

203
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:33,841
[tense music playing]

204
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:35,926
[in Russian] Last week we were in Kazan.

205
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:41,891
[in Russian] We met with our colleagues
by the Lenin statue in Gorky Park.

206
00:10:41,974 --> 00:10:43,059
- [in English] Good.
- [Russian] They're quite the characters.

207
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:44,310
[in Russian] We discussed some business.

208
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:47,021
[in Russian] But some strange things
are happening there.

209
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:48,648
[in English] Very nice.

210
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:50,566
[in English] Uh, Mr. Ambassador, uh…

211
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:53,361
[in Russian] Excuse me,
where is the restroom?

212
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:54,445
‪Ah.

213
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:55,529
[in Russian]

214
00:10:56,113 --> 00:10:57,365
- [in Russian] Oh, to the right.
- [Viktor, in Russian] To the right, yes.

215
00:10:57,448 --> 00:10:58,366
[in English] Thank you.

216
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:10,503
[music fades]

217
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:12,797
Where are you now, Atoy?

218
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:15,674
I'm already worried.

219
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,551
[pensive music playing]

220
00:11:17,635 --> 00:11:18,803
[clicks tongue]

221
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,179
Annoying!

222
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:32,358
[tense music playing]

223
00:12:12,231 --> 00:12:16,068
[device blipping]

224
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:39,633
[in English] Hey! What are you doing here?

225
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:41,469
[rock music playing]

226
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:42,428
Uh…

227
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:46,474
[in English] I-I-I look for toilet.
Toilet.

228
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:49,393
[in English] Sir, there are
no toilets here. None.

229
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:52,771
[in English] Oh, yes. Uh, I know.

230
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:54,732
[in English] I know. No, no, no toilet.

231
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:56,734
[in English] I'll go.
I cannot see a toilet here.

232
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:59,612
[in English] Sir, you are acting
very suspicious.

233
00:12:59,695 --> 00:13:01,447
[in English] I will have to tell
the ambassador.

234
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:03,282
- [in English] Come on.
- [in English] Hey, hey, hey, hey!

235
00:13:03,365 --> 00:13:04,783
[in English] You-You get
your hands off me!

236
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:06,827
[in English] You idiot!
Why are you holding me?

237
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:09,580
[in English] I'm just looking
for the toilet

238
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:12,041
because I'm gonna pee-pee, huh!

239
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:14,210
[in English] You--
So you cannot do that to me! I am--

240
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:17,880
[mumbling]

241
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:19,757
- [grunts]
- [Kurt panicking] Alexei!

242
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,634
- [in English] Brother.
- What are you doing to my brother, huh?!

243
00:13:21,717 --> 00:13:23,260
- [in English] What did you do?
- [in English] Your brother is the one

244
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:24,595
- who hurt me first!
- [in English] Brother.

245
00:13:24,678 --> 00:13:27,348
[in English] That man! That man
don't make me wanna go pee-pee!

246
00:13:27,431 --> 00:13:28,766
[in English] Sir,
what did you do to our guest?

247
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:31,060
[in English] I did nothing to this man!

248
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:33,062
[in English] He attacked me
when I called him out!

249
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:34,730
- [Kurt, in English] He attacked you?
- [in English] Yes!

250
00:13:34,813 --> 00:13:36,857
- [in English] My brother attacked you?!
- [Samir, in English] Yes.

251
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,442
- [in English] Look at him.
- [Atoy coughs]

252
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:42,154
[in English] He is weak, like a baby!
No, like a little girl!

253
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:45,199
[in English] He won't attack you!
He's so old.

254
00:13:45,282 --> 00:13:47,701
- [coughs]
- [in English] You do not smell him now?

255
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:51,497
[in English] His breath
smells like wet dog and mothballs.

256
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:53,499
[in English] It's terrible.
All day, all night,

257
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:55,543
- I smell him. It's--
- [in English] Brother!

258
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,378
[in English] It's so bad! Look.
You are a liar.

259
00:13:57,461 --> 00:14:00,256
- [in English] He didn't attack you! Why?
- [English] I'm not feeling well.

260
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:01,173
[in English] I want to--

261
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:02,967
[sneaky music playing]

262
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:04,552
[in English] Are you okay, Alexei?

263
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:06,470
[in English] Okay, let's go.

264
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:09,890
[music fades]

265
00:14:14,436 --> 00:14:17,106
Where did this fabric come from?
There's no match.

266
00:14:21,735 --> 00:14:24,488
Atoy sewed a suit last night.

267
00:14:24,572 --> 00:14:26,615
Ah… Where is it?

268
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:30,786
There's no fabric like that
among the fittings.

269
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:34,540
He already used what he sewed.
He has a new mission.

270
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:37,209
[in English] Mission?

271
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:39,795
Atoy has a mission?

272
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:41,422
[sneaky music playing]

273
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:47,595
Is this it? These are the scraps
he used for his disguise in…

274
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:51,974
It's huge--

275
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:54,935
[in English] Forty-six, chest.

276
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:56,478
Fifty-one at the be--

277
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:00,900
It's huge-- Did Atoy swallow a ball?

278
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:02,735
Ah! [smirks]

279
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:05,404
I know this.

280
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:09,325
Atoy is pretending to be pregnant.

281
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:11,201
- Hmm? Isn't it?
- [quirky sting]

282
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:13,037
Only someone with a big belly
could wear this.

283
00:15:13,537 --> 00:15:14,663
One with a big, big stomach.

284
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:17,458
Would a pregnant woman wear a suit?

285
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:19,835
Of course, it's Atoy!

286
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:20,878
[smirks]

287
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:24,882
He should have just brought me along.
I could easily be his assistant there.

288
00:15:24,965 --> 00:15:26,800
I could pretend to be…

289
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:29,511
uh, the husband of the pregnant woman.
Yes, I'm the husband.

290
00:15:29,595 --> 00:15:30,763
I'll accompany him to give birth,

291
00:15:30,846 --> 00:15:32,640
- or maybe for a check-up, right?
- [Ame] No!

292
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:36,143
They might not believe
you're the father. Atoy might fail!

293
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:37,978
- [cackles]
- [quirky sting]

294
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:40,522
[in English] Wow!

295
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:43,651
- I'm so embarrassed for you, Ame! Hmm?
- [quirky sting]

296
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,235
[chuckles]

297
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:47,947
Move aside. I'm sweeping.

298
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:50,532
Okay. I'll move-- I'll move aside.

299
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:51,575
Mmm, hmm.

300
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:52,868
There. I'll help you.

301
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:54,578
Here's the dustpan.

302
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:58,332
- Go back to your tailoring shop!
- [chuckles]

303
00:15:58,415 --> 00:15:59,249
Miss!

304
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,001
[in English] I'm not feeling well, uh--

305
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:03,045
- [in English] Like, I feel sick.
- [Kurt] Oh.

306
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:07,299
[in English] There is negative energy
in this office!

307
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,926
- [Atoy sighs]
- [man] All right.

308
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:11,220
- [inaudible]
- [in Russian] What's going on here?

309
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:14,640
- [device blips]
- Oh, oh!

310
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:17,726
[in English] Mr. Ambassador. [chuckles]

311
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,104
[in English] Sir, this man…

312
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:21,855
[in English] This man harassed me!

313
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:24,233
[in English] You know,
you see, I'm an old man, and I…

314
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:26,527
I… I forget where the toilet is.

315
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:29,905
[in English] Here or there, or here,
there. But he's mad at me!

316
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,198
[soft rock music playing]

317
00:16:31,281 --> 00:16:34,576
[in Russian] I am sorry.
[in English] Really, really sorry.

318
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:37,121
- [in English] Sit, brother. Sit.
- [groaning]

319
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:39,289
[in English] So much shame.

320
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:40,791
[in English] Negative energy!

321
00:16:40,874 --> 00:16:42,001
- [spits]
- [Atoy groans]

322
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:44,545
- [in English] Let's go.
- [Atoy groans]

323
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:47,464
[in English] Andrei, Brother,
do not leave me, Brother.

324
00:16:47,548 --> 00:16:48,799
[in English] Thank you.

325
00:16:48,882 --> 00:16:49,717
[tense music playing]

326
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:52,302
[in English] He was hitting me first.

327
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,223
- [elevator dings]
- [Atoy] Come on, come on.

328
00:16:56,306 --> 00:16:58,308
- Come on, come on.
- [in English] Safe to leave?

329
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:01,061
[in English] What are we
gonna do now? What--

330
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:02,855
- What if they find out who we are?
- Anyway.

331
00:17:02,938 --> 00:17:04,481
So, if there's a problem
with the elevator,

332
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:06,066
we won't get through. Let's go.

333
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,360
Where did you lose your ID badge, Sir Ben?

334
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:12,114
If I knew, I would have found it already.

335
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:13,365
How's that?

336
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:15,200
I can't get inside.

337
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:17,077
I still have duty the day after.

338
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:19,413
How long does it take to replace it?

339
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:20,497
[tense music playing]

340
00:17:20,581 --> 00:17:23,083
But we're on rotation tomorrow.

341
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,002
[security guard] Never mind.
I'll just notify

342
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:27,796
my replacement at the service entrance.

343
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,714
[device blips]

344
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:31,842
[Ben] Okay, okay. Just make sure
the spelling is correct.

345
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:33,260
Ben Laput.

346
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:35,888
It's letter U, not letter O.

347
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:37,556
[softly] Let's go, let's go.

348
00:17:45,105 --> 00:17:46,774
[Atoy] That was great, what we did.

349
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:48,275
[muffled chattering]

350
00:17:48,358 --> 00:17:49,234
Oh, hey!

351
00:17:51,695 --> 00:17:54,114
Where did you come from?
Why are you together?

352
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:59,369
Uh, ‘Son, I'll tell you later, okay.

353
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,456
Go shampoo your hair. It'll come off.

354
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:04,541
- [in English] Okay, okay.
- [Atoy] All good?

355
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:06,251
[in English] Ah, stop! Wait a minute.

356
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,128
[sneaky music playing]

357
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:11,673
So-- You were together on the mission?

358
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,300
[in English] Emerson,
you should have seen it!

359
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:15,844
[in English] It was amazing!
We almost got caught!

360
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,721
I was so nervous.

361
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:21,850
I didn't know if I was going to throw up
or faint from nerves.

362
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:24,186
[in English] What?

363
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:26,730
[in English] Come on!

364
00:18:27,731 --> 00:18:29,691
You two, together?
Why didn't you bring me?

365
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:32,236
You, you got to join! Who are you?

366
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:33,445
[in English] Goldilocks?

367
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:34,947
Why did he get to join?

368
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,490
Me-- Atoy, me--

369
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:37,991
You can count on me, Atoy.

370
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:39,952
- Bring me along next time!
- [in English] Emerson, relax, relax.

371
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:40,953
I told you already.

372
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:42,913
- No!
- I told you--

373
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:45,332
- Told you?
- Next time, I'll bring you.

374
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:47,417
[mutters]

375
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:48,752
You might not bring me.

376
00:18:48,836 --> 00:18:51,088
I'll bring you. Next time, promise.

377
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,298
- [in English] Promise, okay.
- Yes.

378
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:54,925
I got you. You and me, right?

379
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:56,135
Okay.

380
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,263
Thank you so much for all your help.

381
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,598
You were amazing.
You improvised so well earlier.

382
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:03,475
- I'm really impressed.
- [in English] Thank you, Atoy. Thank you.

383
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:06,228
I just-- I can't believe
this is your work.

384
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:07,604
Wow, it's like--

385
00:19:08,105 --> 00:19:11,775
It's very impressive, but also… scary.

386
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:14,903
[in English] But I never
felt so alive before.

387
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:16,405
- [grunts]
- [Atoy] It's fine.

388
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:19,908
Just don't think about it too much.
Life goes on here in Tabang Lupa.

389
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,034
- [Kurt, in English] Yes.
- [in English] Secret.

390
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,578
[in English] I don't know, Atoy.

391
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:25,247
[in English] I don't know if I can ever
go back to normal after today, but…

392
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:26,999
[in English] I'm just happy
that I could help.

393
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:28,792
Till next time.

394
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,169
[Emerson] What do you mean till next time?
It's not like that, Brother Kurt.

395
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,421
[in English] Give chance to others!
I'm the others, oh!

396
00:19:32,504 --> 00:19:35,883
[in English] Oh? Atoy, actually,
specifically, if you need, in the future,

397
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:39,636
like, uh, a white dude
or, like, a foreign guy,

398
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:43,098
uh, you just let me know.
Anything Emerson can't do, I'm there.

399
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:44,558
- [in English] You just let me know.
- [Atoy chuckles]

400
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:46,393
- [Atoy] Okay. I'll count on that.
- [Kurt] Okay.

401
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:47,519
- [in English] Thank you.
- Okay.

402
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:50,063
[sneaky music playing]

403
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:50,981
‪[quirky sting]

404
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,364
Emerson, okay.

405
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,574
Do better next time, okay.

406
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:01,867
You're in the mission.

407
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:03,702
In the frustration.

408
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,168
[Atoy] Here, sir, there's CCTV there.

409
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:13,962
In the other corner, there's another one.

410
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:18,091
Then here, at the south entry,
there are two guards.

411
00:20:18,175 --> 00:20:20,886
Here, at the west entry,
there's one, and here,

412
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,306
right in front of the ambassador's office,

413
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:25,807
there are three.

414
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:27,976
[in English] I'm not shocked.

415
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,519
It's an embassy.

416
00:20:30,103 --> 00:20:32,814
The place is certainly highly secured.

417
00:20:34,858 --> 00:20:39,404
The question now is,
how do we extract the laptop?

418
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:41,323
Look at this.

419
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:43,909
[keyboard clacks]

420
00:20:43,992 --> 00:20:45,035
See this window?

421
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:47,996
There's a platform outside this window.

422
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:53,293
Ben, he has access to that platform.

423
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:55,462
He's the window cleaner of the building.

424
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:59,675
My plan is, Ben will be my next identity.

425
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,721
If it's hard to enter the building
from the inside,

426
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:07,140
I'll do it from the outside.

427
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:09,559
How will you do that?

428
00:21:09,643 --> 00:21:12,104
Sir, the building's facade is all glass.

429
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:17,025
What I'll do is make a small hole,
just enough to get in.

430
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:22,364
That's the ninth floor.
Isn't that dangerous?

431
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:25,409
You'll be exposed. Someone might see you.

432
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:26,910
[in English] I know, sir.

433
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:32,249
That's why I accepted this job,
even if it's hard.

434
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,836
Because our national security
will be in danger

435
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:38,046
if we don't retrieve this laptop.

436
00:21:38,755 --> 00:21:40,090
[tense music playing]

437
00:21:46,763 --> 00:21:50,142
[Cita mutters]

438
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:58,734
You seem to be hanging around
the tailoring shop more often.

439
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:01,737
I don't know if you
don't have customers or…

440
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:04,072
you don't have food at home?

441
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:09,953
- Hmm?
- I'm just passing the time, miss.

442
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:12,164
So I won't get bored.

443
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:17,544
And I'm also waiting for Atoy. Maybe…

444
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:21,214
he can bring me along
on his missions, his errands.

445
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:23,133
Mm-hmm. Oh, that's it.
That will be good for you.

446
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:24,760
Hm-mm.

447
00:22:26,386 --> 00:22:27,387
- [knocks]
- [Cita mutters]

448
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:28,388
Hello.

449
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:30,557
[Cita] Oh. Oh. Come in, come in, come in.

450
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:34,686
- [gentle music playing]
- Um, is Atoy here?

451
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:35,896
Atoy?

452
00:22:36,396 --> 00:22:38,565
Uh, do you need something from him?

453
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:42,986
Um, I've been calling him,
but he doesn't answer.

454
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,322
He hangs up on me.

455
00:22:45,822 --> 00:22:48,325
[in English] I just want to make sure
that he's okay.

456
00:22:48,825 --> 00:22:50,160
Ah!

457
00:22:50,243 --> 00:22:51,953
You're just being suspicious.

458
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:53,955
Atoy is just busy.

459
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:56,249
[in English] Busy?

460
00:22:56,333 --> 00:23:01,546
You mean, he's on a tracking mission?

461
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:03,006
[pensive music playing]

462
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:04,508
Uh-huh.

463
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:06,510
[sighs]

464
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:08,845
I thought something happened to him.

465
00:23:09,971 --> 00:23:12,682
Um… Hi!

466
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:17,395
Um, you're the one
who picked up Ibyang the other day, right?

467
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:19,564
[music fades]

468
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:21,066
How is she?

469
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:26,154
Well, she's been crying
for several nights.

470
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:29,074
She said Atoy doesn't want her anymore.

471
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:33,829
Ibyang and I talked about it.
I can't believe it!

472
00:23:33,912 --> 00:23:37,082
Because I know Atoy loves her very much.

473
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:41,711
But Ame said maybe someone
just influenced Atoy,

474
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,296
that's why he changed his decision.

475
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:44,756
[somber music playing]

476
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:47,175
If you can't let go of Ibyang,

477
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:49,261
I won't force you.

478
00:23:49,344 --> 00:23:51,096
But we can't be together

479
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:54,474
if you can't choose our child.

480
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:56,476
[Ibyang] You chose Janine?

481
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:00,981
You won't adopt me anymore?

482
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:03,024
Is she here now?

483
00:24:04,192 --> 00:24:05,986
Can I see her?

484
00:24:06,069 --> 00:24:08,697
[music fades]

485
00:24:19,916 --> 00:24:21,918
[Kurt, in English] <i>I've served</i>
<i>so many beef stew.</i>

486
00:24:22,002 --> 00:24:23,295
[in English] Besides Atoy, I think

487
00:24:23,378 --> 00:24:25,255
you're the only one
I've ever seen who does it like that.

488
00:24:25,338 --> 00:24:26,548
[in English] You're almost
like brother and sister.

489
00:24:26,631 --> 00:24:28,008
[Nestor] You said it, Brother Kurt!

490
00:24:28,091 --> 00:24:30,844
You'd really think Atoy
is Karla's brother.

491
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:32,888
- Mm.
- They even have the same eyes.

492
00:24:32,971 --> 00:24:34,472
‪UP NEXT

493
00:24:34,556 --> 00:24:35,849
Just a warning.

494
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:37,976
What we're about to do is dangerous.

495
00:24:38,476 --> 00:24:42,314
The national security
of our country depends on this.

496
00:24:42,397 --> 00:24:44,149
We will defend the nation.

497
00:24:44,232 --> 00:24:45,317
I will be a hero.

498
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:47,652
- Prepare yourself.
- Is it still him?

499
00:24:47,736 --> 00:24:50,155
[Samir clicks tongue, in English]
I want you to check his profile.

500
00:24:50,238 --> 00:24:54,242
[in English] His name is Alexei Sokolov.

501
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:57,120
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

502
00:24:57,204 --> 00:24:58,830
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

503
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:02,500
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

504
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:03,752
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

505
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:05,712
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
